  "body": "## What\n\nThe first Fort Dearborn's powder magazine (`first_fort_dearborn_magazine`) gets the\n**barrel vault** the owner adopted on 2026-11-03 (T-3335/T-3041), replacing its\nreconstructed gable. One visible correction; nothing else in the fort moves.\n\n## Why, and what the pictures actually say\n\nBoth pinned images were fetched and **read directly** for this change, not taken on trust\nfrom the handoff prose:\n\n| source | sha256 | what it shows |\n|---|---|---|\n| Whistler's measured draught, 25 Jan 1808 (`whistler_1808_fort_dearborn_draught`, his index no. 4) | `4568caac\u202672bfb1` | the magazine in elevation with an **arched front** springing from its side walls, a doorway under it and a small square vent in the tympanum |\n| Currey, *The Story of Old Fort Dearborn* (1912), p. 27 (`currey_1912_first_fort_birdseye`, its no. 8) | `2f2b1e60\u202660a1f` | the same building under a **rounded vault**, at the west end of the north side |\n\n`roof_type` moves from `gable`/`reconstructed` to `barrel_vault`/`inferred`, cited to both.\n\n**The shape is adopted; the curve's depth is NOT matched, and the record says so.** Neither\npicture supplies a radius, a rise, a thickness, a colour, a roofing fabric or a completion\ndate, and none was invented to supply one:\n\n* `barrel_rise_m` = **1.0286254881847008 m**, `reconstructed`. This is *envelope\n  conservation*, not a measurement: half the shorter unchanged 3.05 m plan span times\n  tan(34\u00b0), which holds the crown at **3.628625488184701 m** \u2014 exactly where the old\n  reconstructed gable's peak stood.\n* That makes a **shallow** circular segment, radius **2.9860699863584146 m**. Whistler draws\n  something much closer to a semicircle. We did not follow him there, because matching his\n  arch would raise the crown ~1.2 m above a height nothing attests. **That gap is stated as\n  an open limit, not closed.**\n* The obsolete `roof_pitch_deg` **leaves the record**: a curved roof has a varying tangent,\n  so a single pitch figure would state something the mesh does not contain. The old 34\u00b0\n  survives only inside the derivation note.\n* The one edge that moves is the **side eave**: the same circle run out to the existing\n  0.30 m projection sits at 2.188061556 m instead of the gable's 2.397647445 m, **0.209586 m\n  lower**. Footprint and overall base-to-crown envelope are unchanged.\n\nUnchanged: surveyed seat, bearing, phase dates, 4.51 m front, 3.05 m depth, 2.6 m wall,\nbrick material, openings, covering, material and colour, every other building, and the\nhistorical camera. **Nothing is carried to the second fort's magazine**, which keeps its gable.\n\n## How\n\nAn **opt-in `barrel_vault` branch** in the `fort_structure` archetype: a closed covering\n(underside, front and rear fascia, the two outer side eaves \u2014 no internal ribs), one\ncontinuous height tone rather than per-strip paint, and brick end infills wound outward\n(front +Y, rear \u2212Y) above the unchanged rectangular walls. The 32 arc facets are a mesh\nresolution, not a historical count.\n\nThe parameter check **refuses rather than clamps**. Probed directly, every one of these is\nrejected: a rise that is `None`, zero, negative, NaN, inf, subnormal `1e-320`, a bool, or at\nor above half the width; a vault with a chimney, gallery, cupola, lantern, loopholes or a\nsecond storey; a vault on any kind but `magazine`; and `barrel_rise_m` set on a gable.\n\n## Native rebuild \u2014 done BEFORE the first source commit\n\nThe producer change reaches **25 `fort_structure` defaults and 0 variants** (roster derived\nfrom the records, and it matches the manifest exactly). All 25 were genuinely rebuilt on\n**pinned, sha256-verified Blender 4.5.3** (`975c58fc\u202672d845`) under **Ubuntu 26.04.1 LTS**,\nand the web derivatives re-encoded from that build.\n\n* **Exactly ONE master moved a byte** \u2014 this magazine's. The other **24 came back\n  byte-identical**, including the second fort's magazine (`fort_dearborn_magazine__brick_1816.glb`)\n  and the cupola blockhouse (`fort_dearborn_blockhouse__log_1816.glb`).\n* Re-deriving all 25 web outputs changed exactly **one** web file, so the 24 unchanged\n  masters keep their genuinely bound derivatives.\n* Every fort asset's `inputs_sha256` changes, because the archetype's own source is part of\n  a mesh's inputs. Those are **real freshness hashes from a real build**, never hand-written.\n* **All 243 outbuilding masters, their web derivatives and registry rows are untouched**, as\n  is the T-3041 north-east pyramid. No outbuilding, common, emit or pin edit; no unrelated\n  rebake. No foreign registry row moved.\n\n## Before/after, and the match record\n\nA real **same-camera** comparison through the existing fourteen-member Currey group camera\n(`first_fort_dearborn_pickets_outer`, scene 1812), rendered from the committed GLBs \u2014 the old\nmesh restored for the \"before\" leg and the new one for the \"after\". A pixel comparison of the\ntwo renders changes **only this building** (a single region, x 1512\u20131591, y 111\u2013174); the\nstraight ridge and two flat planes are gone and the roof reads as a continuous curve. The\nprevious render is kept beside the new one as\n`currey_1912_birdseye-side-by-side-before-magazine-vault-20261104.jpg`.\n\nOn `currey_1912_birdseye.match.json` the **magazine difference alone** moves to `fixed`.\n**Verdict stays `differs`.** Still `open`: the blockhouse cupolas and the western gateway.\nOwner-ruling rows are retained untouched.\n\n## Verification\n\n* `tools/check.sh --part 1/4`, `2/4`, `3/4` \u2014 **PASS**, 292 steps each, none red.\n* `tools/check.sh --part 4/4` \u2014 one red, **pre-existing and environmental, not from this\n  diff**: `Selected upper-lid source preserves 925/eyeUV/hoof ownership \u2026 (T-3088)` dies in\n  `tools/transport/horse_socket_interface_v1/socket_controls.py` with\n  `ValueError: Both input arrays must be (arrays of) 3-dimensional vectors` \u2014 NumPy 2 removed\n  2-D `np.cross`, and this runner has numpy 2.5.4. **No input that step reads is in this\n  diff**, it fails identically on the unmodified files, and this repo's own\n  `chicago-4d-check.yml` is green on `dev`. Reporting it rather than reading it as a pass.\n* Staleness is clean (`1034 asset(s) match their inputs, 0 stale`), so the bake and the\n  record agree.\n* `tools/changelog-entries.mjs --check` \u2014 OK.\n* Smoke by parts and both viewports: see the comment below.\n\n## Bookkeeping\n\n`docs/LIBERTIES.md` gains `L-first-fort-magazine-barrel-vault-3041`, which admits the rise,\nthe radius, the shallow-vs-semicircle gap, the projection, the covering edge and the facet\ncount. L370's two now-dangling claims on this record (`form.roof_pitch_deg`, `form.roof_type`)\nare dropped from its `Covers:` list and the reason is written into the new entry's\n**Supersedes:** note \u2014 the same move `L-first-fort-ne-house-pyramid-3041` made in PR #1685.\n`docs/STATUS.md` gains a T-3041 section stating the limits. `docs/ROADMAP.md` is the frozen\nreasoning archive and is deliberately not touched.\n\n## What this is NOT\n\n**T-3041 and parent T-2387 stay OPEN and PARTIAL.** This is one difference of thirteen on one\npicture. The full first-fort acceptance \u2014 21 named records, nine context records, every listed\npicture \u2014 is untouched. No whole-fort match is claimed, no photo follow-up ticket is filed, no\nsplit, no `done --anyway`. The ticket is released OPEN with its remaining differences.\n\n### A note on the claim\n\n`ticket.mjs claim T-3041` first refused, naming `steward/t3041-parade-presence-20261104` as a\nrival branch. That branch is a **landed leftover**: its PR #1696 merged into `dev` at\n2026-11-04T05:13:53Z and its remote head still equals that PR's head exactly, with no claim on\nthe ticket (`claimed_by`, `claimed_run`, `claimed_at`, `pr` all null) and no open PR carrying\nT-3041. That is the documented stale-branch case the tool's own message points at, so the\nclaim was taken with `--force` after checking \u2014 not past a live owner.\n\n\ud83e\udd16 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
